# Infrastructure rules

- Keep local, test, staging and production configuration/credentials separate.
- `.env.example` contains names/placeholders only; never real secrets.
- Database/Redis should not be publicly exposed in production.
- Production services use least privilege/non-root containers where practical.
- Add health/readiness checks and bounded resource settings for production services.
- TLS/public ingress terminates through reviewed reverse proxy/CDN/WAF layer.
- Do not assume Docker Compose development settings are production-safe.
- Backups, restore testing and migration safety are part of production readiness.
- Production AI/payment/admin secrets are injected by secret management/runtime environment, not image/build args/client env.
